          "key": "raise-concurrency",
          "kind": "suggestion",
          "name": "raise-concurrency",
          "near": false,
          "plan": [
            "then (prediction): KV-cache capacity likely binds next (watch for KV-cache usage near full with requests waiting)",
            "then (prediction): `more-kv-memory`, after which queueing before scheduling likely binds next (watch for requests waiting at the concurrency cap)"
          ],
          "quality_risk": false,
          "reason": "running requests hit max_concurrent_requests 8 with 120 waiting, and the highest sampled KV-cache usage is only 23.2%; at your declared load of 128 concurrent clients, up to 128 requests were in flight, so 16 is worth trying (the load is what your configuration declares, not measured traffic). It usually cuts queueing (TTFT) but slows each token (TPOT) as more sequences share every step - measure both",
          "test": "about 7 min on this setup (this run: 60 s to load, 6.1 min to warm up and measure)",
          "tier": "try_first"
        },
        {
          "audience": "all",
